{"repositoryId":482145441,"availability":"available","full":"kking935/Blockin-Demo","name":"Blockin-Demo","description":"🔐 Welcome to the Blockin Demo! Blockin is a JavaScript library built to provide a flexible foundation for resource providers to implement role-based access control, dynamic resource owner privileges, and expiration tokens on-chain through a two-step process.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2022-04-16T03:30:58Z","updated":"2026-04-27T08:51:57Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://blockin.vercel.app","topics":["blockchain","nextjs","serverless","walletconnect"],"demo":"https://blockin.vercel.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T23:48:24.002Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T23:48:24.002Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T23:48:24.002Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T23:48:24.002Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A reference implementation of Blockin — a library for on-chain role-based access control using NFTs as authorization tokens.","This demo shows the full Blockin flow against Algorand (testnet) and Ethereum / Polygon / BSC / Avalanche (mainnet), including:","Status: archival. This demo was built in 2022 against Algorand's Purestake API and Moralis v1. Purestake's API was shut down in December 2023 and Moralis v1 is deprecated, so the live flow no longer runs without a dependency refresh. The code is preserved as a reference for the Blockin protocol pattern."],"features":["Creating authorization assets on-chain","Signing a challenge with a connected wallet","Verifying ownership of the asset via blockchain lookup","Granting access to a gated resource for the duration the asset is held"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kking935/Blockin-Demo/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c203c0396d3eedf9bc84842fb3aa4f51ab9e5f62421358cbb4c65bbc713832f8","extractedAt":"2026-10-16T23:48:24.103Z"},"ove